---
.title = "Bound a network receive with a timeout",
.date = "2026-09-29",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

Blocking network reads need a deadline so an idle peer cannot hold a task forever.
`std.Io.net.Socket.receiveTimeout` returns `error.Timeout` when no UDP datagram arrives
before the deadline. The same timeout policy can be applied around other network operations
that support `std.Io.Timeout`.

